```java
interface FeeCalculator { BigDecimal calculate(ParkingTicket t, LocalDateTime exit); }

class HourlyFeeCalculator implements FeeCalculator {
    private static final BigDecimal RATE = new BigDecimal("5.00");
    public BigDecimal calculate(ParkingTicket t, LocalDateTime exit) {
        long hrs = Math.max(1, Duration.between(t.entry(), exit).toHours());
        return RATE.multiply(BigDecimal.valueOf(hrs)); // BigDecimal for money, never double
    }
}

class ParkingLot {
    private FeeCalculator feeCalculator;                 // swappable at runtime
    void setFeeCalculator(FeeCalculator c) { this.feeCalculator = c; }
    BigDecimal unpark(ParkingTicket t) { return feeCalculator.calculate(t, LocalDateTime.now()); }
}
```
*A new pricing model = a new class implementing the interface. `ParkingLot` never changes.*

