```java
class ParkingSpot {
    // CAS holder: set succeeds only if currently null
    private final AtomicReference<Vehicle> vehicle = new AtomicReference<>();
    boolean isFree() { return vehicle.get() == null; }
    boolean park(Vehicle v) { return vehicle.compareAndSet(null, v); } // true = I won
}
// Lock-free: if two threads race, exactly one compareAndSet returns true.
// Equivalent with a lock: a synchronized park() method also works for fresher level.
```
*Store spots in a `ConcurrentHashMap`, and lock per-spot (or per-floor) — never the whole lot.*
